## Realize it as a Dockerfile

Author a Dockerfile installing the inferred libc/loader pair and preserving
interpreter, arch, permissions, and the hardening both sources describe, served
over the declared protocol. Do not bend the runtime to fit the historical
exploit — the exploit is re-fitted to the runtime, not the reverse.

## When neither source pins the runtime

If the writeup names no concrete runtime fact and the exploit hardcodes no libc
offset, emit `status: blocked` with a `runtime_inference_unsupported` blocker
citing both sources' gaps; do not upgrade prose into a glibc minor version.

